course: dictionary
lesson: 11790
title: Words with belly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «bellied» comes from «belly», which means tummy. You will often see it joined to another word with a dash, like «pot-bellied». The first word tells you what kind of belly it is. A pot-belly is round and sticks out.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. «The red-bellied woodpecker tapped on the old tree.» Red-bellied tells you the bird has a red tummy. Swap in your meaning to check: a bird with a red tummy makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Bellied can also mean swelled out in a round shape. «The sails bellied in the wind.» Sails do not have tummies, so the clue is the wind. The sails puffed out round, like a full belly. Ask what word would fit, then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Belly-up is a different phrase. «The fish floated belly-up in the pond» means the fish had died. When a word is new, read the words around it first, and use a dictionary if the clues are not enough.
fact: Bellied comes from belly, which means tummy.
fact: «Pot-bellied» means having a round, sticking-out tummy, as in «The pot-bellied pig snored in the sun.»
fact: «Red-bellied» and «yellow-bellied» often appear in the names of birds and animals, such as the red-bellied woodpecker.
fact: «The sails bellied out as the wind blew.» Here bellied means swelled out in a round shape.
fact: Talk about bodies kindly. A round tummy is just one kind of body. Yellow-bellied is an old slang word meaning cowardly, and it is not a kind word to use about people.
exercise: «The pot-bellied pig snored in the sun.» What does pot-bellied describe? | Its muddy feet | Its loud, happy grunt | Its curly tail | *Its tummy, which is round and sticks out
exercise: Sara sees a bird and says, «It is a red-bellied woodpecker.» What does red-bellied tell you? | *It has a red tummy | It has red wings | It likes to sing at night
exercise: «The sails bellied out as the wind blew.» What does bellied mean here? | *Swelled out in a round shape | Torn into little pieces | Turned a bright colour | Fell into the sea
test: «The fish floated belly-up in the pond.» What does belly-up mean for a fish? | It is hiding | *It has died | It is hungry | It is swimming fast
test: Which sentence uses bellied to mean swelled out? | «The yellow-bellied bird was singing.» | «The big-bellied bear was asleep.» | *«The sails bellied out in the strong wind.»
exam: What does the word «bellied» come from, and what does it usually describe? | A word for legs, and how fast something runs | *The word belly, a tummy, and what kind of belly something has | A word for head, and what kind of hair something has
